    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work front and back body panels as for a standard drop-shoulder tunic. When seaming the sides, begin the seam 15 cm above the hem and work up to the underarm, leaving the lower 15 cm of each side unjoined as a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "side-vent-g69"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "side vent"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Finish each vent edge with a dc edging. Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "dc2tog-g69"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "dc2tog"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " at the front neck."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Size M: panels 146 sts wide and 81.7 cm tall. Side seam begins 24 rows up from hem (approximately 15 cm)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
